《中秋的灯》 The Mid-Autumn Lantern — Paper-cut Lightbox 纸雕灯影

Story, picture, score and sound are made in code in this folder. Every paper layer, the village, the sea, the lighthouse,
the figures and the lanterns are drawn by src/ (a Canvas2D paper compositor: backlight, cast shadows, depth of field, bloom).
No photos, footage, generated images or voices are used. The village, its people and the lighthouse are fiction.

Music (written for this film; played on sampled instruments by core/audio/sampler.py and synthesized by core/audio/pluck.py and mix.py)
- Piano: "Salamander Grand Piano V3" by Alexander Holm, licensed under CC BY 3.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/)
  (played soft and low-passed as a felt piano)
- Samples (CC0): VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition (Versilian Studios / Sam Gossner), Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios)
  Instruments: violins, violins tremolo, violas, cellos, cellos spiccato, contrabass, harp, hand chimes, small gong, piano.
- Physical modelling (core/audio/pluck.py, no samples): music box, pipa, guqin.
- Synthesis (mix.py): a bamboo flute (xiao), the beds and all sound effects.

Sound effects
- Procedural (core/audio/sfx.py and mix.py): room tone, lamp hum, sea, wind, fog, village hum, gulls, crickets, switch clicks and
  shimmers for every light, paper slides and rustles, scissor snips, lid, taps, foghorn, radio crackle, lamp buzz, steps on planks
  and stone, wheel creak, window wipe, boat engine, boat bump, fog whooshes.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; fetched from github.com/google/fonts into fonts/)
- Ma Shan Zheng (马善政毛笔楷书) — the title and the paper strips. https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/mashanzheng
- Noto Serif SC — the subtitles (subset to the characters the film uses: fonts/NotoSerifSC-sub.ttf). https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk

Tools
- Headless Chromium (Playwright), ffmpeg 9 (loudness normalisation, encoding), numpy/scipy/soundfile, fontTools (subsetting).
- Lemo-Opuscar core tools: core/render (frame capture, events, reading-time check, srt, mux), core/audio (sampler, pluck, sfx).
